<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mīnōus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		Minos, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Minos, Minoan;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> also for <i>Cretan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Minoa venundata Scylla figura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					4, 18</span></i>
			 (19), 21: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pasiphaë,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the wife of Minos</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thoas,</span>”
				<i>the son of Ariadne</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					6, 114</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harenae,</span>”
				<i>the shores of Crete</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ib.
					511</span></i>
			. </div>
